From cfade36c6ebbb8c12b08554f180f36460d408873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:01:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770: synchronous NAND program/erase, SmartFS self-heal

Programming and erasing returned as soon as the APBH chain had been
handed to the DMA engine.  The file system writes a sector and reads it
back immediately, so with the device still busy the next command aborted
the program: the page stayed erased and every append eventually failed
(EIO) at whatever sector boundary the timing hit.  Bounding the wait
keeps a dead device a failed write instead of a hang.

Board side, from the same hardware session:
- probe the mounted volume with a write/umount/remount/read before
  trusting it, and reformat when it does not survive that;
- when the 3.2 MB engine copy fails, unlink the partial file and run
  from the raw staging area instead of reformatting on every boot;
- wake the shell from inside the application at exit, not from the
  thread trampoline (does not fix the quit hang yet -- see the notes).
---
 arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c         |  31 ++-
 .../arm/stmp3770/hp39gii/src/hp39gii_boot.c   | 227 +++++++++++++++---
 .../hp39gii/src/khicas/khicas_app.cpp         |   8 +
 3 files changed, 234 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

